  "body": {
    "id": "lem:operational-selector-bridge",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "The plug-in frontier \\(\\widehat{\\mathfrak F}_n\\) is a \\(\\mathcal F_n^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\)-measurable random element of \\(C([0,1])\\) and is computable from \\(\\{(X_{ni},A_{ni},Y_{ni}):1\\le i\\le n\\}\\), \\(b\\), and the declared finite-cell estimators, without \\(\\Delta_n\\), \\(u_n\\), or \\(E_n\\). For every \\(\\mathcal F_n^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\)-measurable \\(\\widehat t_n\\) and every real \\(x\\), the deterministic inclusion \\(\\{\\sup_{t\\in[0,1]}T_n(t)\\le x\\}\\subseteq\\{T_n(\\widehat t_n)\\le x\\}\\) holds. On \\(0<\\widehat t_n<1\\), with \\(\\widehat c_n=\\widehat t_n/(1-\\widehat t_n)\\), \\(T_n(\\widehat t_n)=(1+\\widehat c_n)\\sqrt n\\,\\mathscr R_n(\\widehat c_n)\\). Thus a uniform law or simultaneous coverage bound for the oracle path transfers exactly to a selector computed from the plug-in frontier; no approximation of the unobserved regret by \\(\\widehat{\\mathfrak F}_n\\) is required.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Fhat",
      "Fobs",
      "Oobs",
