    ],
    "justification": "The lemma separates the observable frontier used to choose a temperature from the oracle regret path that the confidence envelope covers.",
    "gap": "Post-search arguments such as Kang's assume an observed indexed statistic, while the causal regret here contains an unobserved oracle comparator; the exact event inclusion supplies the needed operational bridge without a false plug-in equality.",
    "consumer": "A planner can compute a temperature from the displayed plug-in frontier and invoke the simultaneous oracle-regret certificate at precisely that observed-data choice.",
    "proof_tex": "Each cell count, cell sum, empirical stratum weight, and hence each coordinate of \\(\\widehat u_n\\) is \\(\\mathcal F_n^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\)-measurable.  The formulas defining the plug-in frontier use only finite arithmetic, maxima, exponentials, logarithms, and the fixed benchmark.  The endpoint lemmas show that the resulting pointwise formula is a continuous path.  Rational-time measurability and separability of \\(C([0,1])\\) then show that \\(\\widehat{\\mathfrak F}_n\\) is an \\(\\mathcal F_n^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\)-measurable random element.  Its displayed construction contains neither \\(\\Delta_n\\), \\(u_n\\), nor \\(E_n\\).\n\nFor every path \\(f\\), every index \\(s\\in[0,1]\\), and every real \\(x\\), \\(\\sup_tf(t)\\le x\\) implies \\(f(s)\\le x\\).  Apply this deterministic fact pointwise with \\(f=T_n\\) and \\(s=\\widehat t_n\\) to obtain\n\\[\n \\{\\sup_tT_n(t)\\le x\\}\\subseteq\\{T_n(\\widehat t_n)\\le x\\}.\n\\]\nNo independence between \\(T_n\\) and the selector is used.  If \\(0<\\widehat t_n<1\\), the exact regret identity with \\(\\widehat c_n=\\widehat t_n/(1-\\widehat t_n)\\) gives\n\\[\n T_n(\\widehat t_n)=(1+\\widehat c_n)\\sqrt n\\,\\mathscr R_n(\\widehat c_n).\n\\]\nThus the observed frontier selects the index, while the covered target remains the oracle causal regret.",
